        <dc:title>It's Like This: 108 Dhamma Similes</dc:title>
        <dc:creator opf:file-as="Chah, Venerable Ajahn" opf:role="aut">Venerable Ajahn Chah</dc:creator>
        <dc:contributor opf:file-as="calibre" opf:role="bkp">calibre (4.9.1) [https://calibre-ebook.com]</dc:contributor>
        <dc:date>2013-05-26T07:00:00+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:description>Venerable Ajahn Chah was a master at using the apt and unusual simile to explain points of Dhamma in a memorable way. He was especially talented at exploiting the open-ended nature of the simile - using a particular image to make one point in one context, and a very different point in another. This book is a companion to In Simple Terms, an earlier collection of similes drawn from Ajahn Chah's transcribed talks.</dc:description>
